"Chest of Preserving,""WDMM"",""139"",""common"",""Wondrous Item"","""","""","""","""",""25 lb."","""",""Food and other perishable items do not age or decay while inside a Chest of Preserving. The chest is 2½ feet long, 1½ feet wide, and 1 foot tall with a half-barrel lid. The chest has a lock, which can be picked with thieves' tools and a successful DC 15 Dexterity check. Smashing the lock or any other part of the chest renders it nonmagical.""";;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
"Chicken,""DMG'24"",""213"",""none"",""Trade Good"","""","""","""","""","""",""2 CP"",""Merchants commonly exchange trade goods without using currency.""";;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
"Chime of Exile,""VEoR"",""46"",""very rare"",""Wondrous Item"","""","""","""","""","""","""",""This silver chime is engraved with delicate magic sigils. While holding the chime, you can use an action to cast the Banishment spell (spell save DC 20). If the target of the spell has 50 hit points or fewer, it automatically fails its saving throw. Once the chime has been used to cast the spell, it can't be used this way again until the next dawn.""";;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
"Chime of Opening,""DMG'24"",""244"",""rare"",""Wondrous Item"","""","""","""","""",""1 lb."","""",""This hollow metal tube measures about 1 foot long and weighs 1 pound. As a Magic action, you can strike the chime to cast Knock. The spell's customary knocking sound is replaced by the clear, ringing tone of the chime, which is audible out to 300 feet. The chime can be used 10 times. After the tenth time, it cracks and becomes useless.""";;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
"Chromatic Rose,""WBtW"",""208"",""rare"",""Wondrous Item"","""","""","""","""","""","""",""This magic rose comes in one of five colors, as noted in the Chromatic Roses table. While a rose is held, it gains a harmless visual effect as indicated on the table.";;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
While holding the rose by its stem, you gain resistance to damage of the type associated with the rose's color. If you would take more than 10 damage of this type from a single source (after applying the resistance), the rose disintegrates, and you take no damage instead.;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
As an action, you can blow the petals from the rose to produce a 20-foot cone of acid, lightning, poisonous gas, fire, or cold, as dictated by the rose's damage type. Each creature in the cone must make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 3d10 damage of the appropriate type on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Using this property destroys the rose.;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
